es (2599); Relationships (2599, 4639)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Clinical Guidelines and Recommendations\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Organizations like the European Association of Enteral and Parenteral Nutrition (ESPEN) and the American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ASPEN) provide essential guidelines for the use of enteral and parenteral nutrition. These guidelines help healthcare professionals determine the appropriate nutritional support for patients based on their specific medical conditions, ensuring that nutritional interventions are tailored to individual needs [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (13681, 2731); Relationships (4811, 264)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Nutritional Formulas and Their Applications\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Various specialized nutritional formulas are designed to meet the unique dietary needs of patients with specific health conditions. These formulas, including polymeric, oligomeric, and elemental types, are crucial for patients with digestive issues, metabolic disorders, or those recovering from surgery. The choice of formula can significantly influence patient recovery and overall health outcomes [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (4876, 4873); Relationships (2659, 2660)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Impact of Medical Conditions on Nutritional Needs\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Certain medical conditions, such as acute renal failure, cancer, and Crohn's disease, necessitate specific nutritional interventions. Enteral nutrition is often employed to stabilize the nutritional status of patients with these conditions, ensuring they receive adequate nutrients to support their recovery. Understanding the interplay between these conditions and nutritional support is essential for effective patient management [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (10081, 1472); Relationships (899, 2775)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Complications Associated with Nutritional Support\",\n            \"explanation\": \"While enteral and parenteral nutrition are critical for patient care, they can also lead to complications. Enteral nutrition may cause digestive symptoms or infections, while parenteral nutrition is associated with risks such as aluminum toxicity and metabolic imbalances. Careful management and monitoring are necessary to mitigate these risks and ensure patient safety [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (11473, 4848); Relationships (4873, 2809)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"The Role of Age in Nutritional Support\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Age significantly influences the nutritional needs and interventions for patients. Elderly patients often require tailored nutritional support due to age-related health considerations, making it essential to adjust enteral nutrition strategies accordingly. This demographic factor is crucial in determining the type and amount of nutritional support provided [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (2535, 2888); Relationships (2889, 2535)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Research Contributions to Nutritional Practices\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Researchers like De Luis Román DA and studies such as those by Kim et al. have significantly contributed to the understanding of enteral and parenteral nutrition. Their work informs best practices and guidelines, enhancing the quality of care provided to patients requiring nutritional support. Ongoing research is vital for advancing nutritional therapies and improving patient outcomes [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (4848, 13368); Relationships (4737, 4804)].\"\n        }\n    ]\n}", "input": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery. Information discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims. The report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact. The content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their legal compliance, technical capabilities, reputation, and noteworthy claims.\n\n# Report Structure\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {{\n        \"title\": <report_title>,\n        \"summary\": <executive_summary>,\n        \"rating\": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": <rating_explanation>,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n----Reports-----\ncommunity,full_content\r\n1178,\"# Nutritional Support Community: Enteral and Parenteral Nutrition\n\nThe Nutritional Support Community focuses on enteral and parenteral nutrition methods essential for patients unable to consume food orally. Key entities include various nutritional methods, medical conditions, and guidelines that interconnect to provide comprehensive patient care.\n\n## Importance of Enteral Nutrition\n\nEnteral nutrition is vital for delivering nutrients directly to patients who cannot consume food orally. It is particularly beneficial for critically ill patients, those with swallowing difficulties, and individuals with chronic illnesses. Enteral nutrition helps maintain the integrity of the intestinal barrier, reduces infection risks, and improves overall nutritional status. This method is preferred over parenteral nutrition when the digestive tract is functional, as it has lower complication rates and better outcomes in critically ill patients [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (347); Relationships (2599, 269, 2640)].\n\n## Role of Parenteral Nutrition\n\nParenteral nutrition is utilized when enteral nutrition is not feasible, providing essential nutrients intravenously. It is crucial for patients with conditions that impair their ability to utilize the digestive tract effectively, such as severe pancreatitis or intestinal obstructions. While parenteral nutrition is necessary in certain cases, it is associated with higher complication rates compared to enteral nutrition, making the choice between the two methods critical based on patient conditions [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (2599); Relationships (2599, 4639)].\n\n## Clinical Guidelines and Recommendations\n\nOrganizations like the European Association of Enteral and Parenteral Nutrition (ESPEN) and the American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ASPEN) provide essential guidelines for the use of enteral and parenteral nutrition. These guidelines help healthcare professionals determine the appropriate nutritional support for patients based on their specific medical conditions, ensuring that nutritional interventions are tailored to individual needs [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (13681, 2731); Relationships (4811, 264)].\n\n## Nutritional Formulas and Their Applications\n\nVarious specialized nutritional formulas are designed to meet the unique dietary needs of patients with specific health conditions. These formulas, including polymeric, oligomeric, and elemental types, are crucial for patients with digestive issues, metabolic disorders, or those recovering from surgery. The choice of formula can significantly influence patient recovery and overall health outcomes [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (4876, 4873); Relationships (2659, 2660)].\n\n## Impact of Medical Conditions on Nutritional Needs\n\nCertain medical conditions, such as acute renal failure, cancer, and Crohn's disease, necessitate specific nutritional interventions. Enteral nutrition is often employed to stabilize the nutritional status of patients with these conditions, ensuring they receive adequate nutrients to support their recovery. Understanding the interplay between these conditions and nutritional support is essential for effective patient management [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (10081, 1472); Relationships (899, 2775)].\n\n## Complications Associated with Nutritional Support\n\nWhile enteral and parenteral nutrition are critical for patient care, they can also lead to complications. Enteral nutrition may cause digestive symptoms or infections, while parenteral nutrition is associated with risks such as aluminum toxicity and metabolic imbalances. Careful management and monitoring are necessary to mitigate these risks and ensure patient safety [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (11473, 4848); Relationships (4873, 2809)].\n\n## The Role of Age in Nutritional Support\n\nAge significantly influences the nutritional needs and interventions for patients. Elderly patients often require tailored nutritional support due to age-related health considerations, making it essential to adjust enteral nutrition strategies accordingly. This demographic factor is crucial in determining the type and amount of nutritional support provided [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (2535, 2888); Relationships (2889, 2535)].\n\n## Research Contributions to Nutritional Practices\n\nResearchers like De Luis Román DA and studies such as those by Kim et al. have significantly contributed to the understanding of enteral and parenteral nutrition. Their work informs best practices and guidelines, enhancing the quality of care provided to patients requiring nutritional support. Ongoing research is vital for advancing nutritional therapies and improving patient outcomes [Data: Reports (2142); Entities (4848, 13368); Relationships (4737, 4804)].\"\r\n1183,\"# Nutritional Formulas and Macronutrients Community\n\nThis community encompasses various nutritional formulas and macronutrients essential for patient care, particularly in enteral nutrition. The entities are interconnected through their roles in providing dietary support for individuals with specific health needs, including pediatric and critical care patients.\n\n## Macronutrients as essential dietary components\n\nMacronutrients, including carbohydrates, proteins, and fats, are fundamental for maintaining health and energy levels. They are crucial in the dietary management of various health conditions, such as cancer and diabetes, where a balanced intake is necessary for optimal patient nutrition. The absorption of these nutrients primarily occurs in the small intestine, highlighting their importance in overall health and nutrition. [Data: Entities (1784, 1889, 1788, 7610, 7611, +more)]\n\n## Diverse range of nutritional formulas\n\nThe community includes a variety of nutritional formulas, such as polymeric, oligomeric, and elemental formulas, each designed for specific patient needs. Polymeric formulas are suitable for patients with adequate gastrointestinal function, while oligomeric formulas are tailored for those with digestive issues. Elemental formulas are highly processed and intended for patients with severe allergies or malabsorption issues. This diversity allows for tailored nutritional support based on individual patient requirements. [Data: Entities (2474, 4879, 2475, 14452, 2476, +more)]\n\n## Importance of enteral nutrition\n\nEnteral nutrition is a method of delivering nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract, which is vital for patients who cannot consume food orally. The various formulas used in enteral nutrition, such as polymeric and oligomeric formulas, are designed to meet the specific dietary needs of patients, ensuring they receive adequate nutrition for recovery and health maintenance. This method is particularly important in critical care settings where patients may have compromised digestive functions. [Data: Relationships (2659, 2660, 2836, 2661, 2682, +more)]\n\n## Role of pediatric formulas\n\nPediatric formulas are specialized nutritional products designed to meet the unique dietary needs of infants and children. These formulas ensure that young patients receive the necessary nutrients for growth and development, particularly in cases where they have specific digestive or absorption issues. The community's focus on pediatric nutrition highlights the importance of tailored dietary solutions for vulnerable populations. [Data: Entities (2469, 10039, 9974, 9975, 9976, +more)]\n\n## Nutritional management in critical care\n\nNutritional management is crucial in critical care settings, where patients often require specialized formulas to support their recovery. Polymeric formulas are commonly recommended for critical patients, as they provide essential nutrients without compromising digestive function. The community's emphasis on critical care nutrition underscores the importance of appropriate dietary interventions in improving patient outcomes. [Data: Relationships (10039, 10040, 10038, 10036, 10035, +more)]\n\n## Health benefits of vegetable oils\n\nVegetable oils are recognized for their health benefits, particularly in promoting cardiovascular health. They are often included in nutritional formulas to provide essential fatty acids and are associated with a lower risk of cardiovascular disease compared to saturated fats. This highlights the community's focus on incorporating healthier dietary fats into nutritional products. [Data: Entities (1889, 7793, 7654, 7792, 2614, +more)]\"\r\n1186,\"# Enteral Nutrition Community: Devices and Medications\n\nThe community focuses on enteral nutrition, involving various medical devices and medications essential for patients unable to consume food orally. Key entities include nasoenteral tubes, enteral feeding tubes, and medications like Metoclopramida, which facilitate nutritional support and manage related complications.\n\n## Importance of Nasoenteral Tubes\n\nThe SONDA NASOENTERAL is a vital medical device used for providing enteral nutrition to patients who cannot eat by mouth. This device is particularly indicated for short-term use and is beneficial for patients with conditions like delayed gastric emptying or a risk of aspiration. The use of nasoenteral tubes is crucial in managing patients' nutritional needs, especially in critical care settings. However, complications such as agitation in patients with decreased consciousness can arise from its use, highlighting the need for careful monitoring and management. [Data: Entities (6845); Relationships (3272, 9490)]\n\n## Role of Metoclopramida in Enteral Nutrition\n\nMetoclopramida is a medication that plays a significant role in enhancing enteral nutrition by promoting gastric emptying and alleviating nausea. It is particularly effective in oncology patients who often experience nausea that can hinder their nutritional intake. The administration of Metoclopramida is essential in critical care settings, where it is used to manage symptoms and improve the overall tolerance of enteral nutrition. However, it is important to note that Metoclopramida may cause diarrhea, which can complicate the nutritional management of patients. [Data: Entities (2282); Relationships (3101, 2806, 9491)]\n\n## Enteral Feeding Tubes as Critical Devices\n\nThe SONDA ENTERAL is a critical device for delivering nutrition directly to the gastrointestinal tract for patients unable to consume food orally. This enteral feeding tube is essential for administering necessary nutrients and is commonly used in various medical settings. The relationship between enteral feeding and the devices used, such as the SONDA NASOENTERAL and SONDA NASOYEYUNAL, underscores the importance of these tools in patient care. Proper placement and management of these tubes are crucial to prevent complications such as aspiration pneumonia. [Data: Entities (1925); Relationships (2625, 6814, 7920)]\n\n## Complications Associated with Enteral Nutrition\n\nNEUMONÍA ASPIRATIVA is a serious complication that can arise from the use of enteral feeding tubes, occurring when food or liquid inadvertently enters the lungs. This condition poses significant risks to patients receiving enteral nutrition, particularly if the feeding tubes are not managed properly. The potential for aspiration pneumonia necessitates strict adherence to protocols for tube placement and monitoring, emphasizing the need for healthcare providers to be vigilant in managing enteral nutrition. [Data: Entities (14574); Relationships (7920, 16096)]\n\n## Interactions Between Medications and Enteral Nutrition\n\nCertain medications, such as Fenitoína and Dicumarínicos, require special precautions when administered with enteral nutrition due to their interactions with feeding tubes. Fenitoína's plasma levels can be significantly reduced when given alongside enteral nutrition, necessitating careful monitoring to ensure therapeutic effectiveness. Similarly, Dicumarínicos need to be administered with caution to prevent incompatibilities. These interactions highlight the importance of understanding the relationships between medications and enteral feeding to optimize patient care. [Data: Entities (14273, 14339); Relationships (2814, 7917)]\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n6716,TRASPLANTE DE CÉLULAS HEMATOPIÉTICAS,\"Hematopoietic cell transplantation, also known as stem cell transplantation, is a medical procedure designed to restore blood cell production in patients suffering from specific diseases. This treatment involves the transplantation of hematopoietic stem cells, which are crucial for generating blood cells. Although hematopoietic stem cell transplantation was considered as a treatment option for the patient, it was ultimately rejected.\",5\r\n1891,SONDA,\"SONDA refers to a medical device utilized for administering enteral nutrition to patients who are unable to feed themselves orally. This device is positioned supradiaphragmatically to facilitate access to the stomach, allowing for the direct delivery of nutrients to the stomach or intestines. The sonda serves as a crucial tool in providing necessary nutrition to individuals requiring medical support for their dietary needs.\",5\r\n12276,TUBO DIGESTIVO,\"The \"\"TUBO DIGESTIVO,\"\" or digestive tract, is a vital anatomical structure responsible for processing food and facilitating digestion and nutrient absorption. It serves as the pathway through which enteral nutrition is administered directly to patients, highlighting its importance in clinical settings. The functionality of the tubo digestivo is crucial for determining the type of nutritional support required, especially in medical conditions such as pancreatitis, where specific nutritional management is necessary. Additionally, the tubo digestivo can be the subject of various diagnostic explorations to assess its health and functionality. Overall, the tubo digestivo plays a central role in both the digestive process and the management of nutritional needs in patients.\",6\r\n9467,ALMIDÓN DE MAÍZ,\"Almidón de maíz, or corn starch, is a carbohydrate derived from corn that serves multiple purposes in nutrition and cooking. It is commonly utilized in enteral nutrition and dietary plans for various age groups, including infants and adults, to help maintain stable blood glucose levels. In addition to its role as a carbohydrate source in nutritional formulas, corn starch is frequently employed as a thickening agent in culinary applications. It is particularly beneficial in dietary treatments for metabolic disorders, where it aids in managing blood glucose levels effectively. Furthermore, corn starch is recommended as a dietary component for patients, especially before sleep, to support the maintenance of healthy blood glucose levels.\",9\r\n10731,GLUCOGENOSIS TIPO I,\"Glucogenosis tipo I is a metabolic disorder affecting the body's ability to break down glycogen, leading to various health complications.\",6\r\n8616,WARFARINA,\"Warfarina is an anticoagulant medication that plays a crucial role in preventing blood clots. It is important to note that Warfarina may interact with weight loss medications, necessitating careful monitoring of patients who are using both. Additionally, the efficacy of Warfarina can be significantly influenced by dietary factors, particularly vitamin K intake, which may counteract its anticoagulant effects. Furthermore, the absorption of Warfarina can be altered by enteral nutrition, potentially impacting its therapeutic action. Certain foods, especially those high in fat, can also decrease the effectiveness of Warfarina. Therefore, patients on Warfarina should be aware of these interactions and dietary considerations to ensure optimal therapeutic outcomes.\",5\r\n13238,ENFERMEDAD VASCULAR CEREBRAL,\"Enfermedad Vascular Cerebral, también conocida como enfermedad cerebrovascular, es una condición que afecta el suministro de sangre al cerebro. Esta enfermedad puede resultar en complicaciones significativas, como la disfasia y la desnutrición, especialmente después de un accidente cerebrovascular. Los problemas de salud y nutrición en los pacientes son comunes debido a la interrupción del flujo sanguíneo, lo que resalta la importancia de una atención adecuada y oportuna para mitigar sus efectos.\",4\r\n15814,EUGLANA ENGLANO,Euglana Englano is another individual referenced in discussions about the ethical and legal implications of withdrawing enteral nutrition in patients with permanent vegetative states.,3\r\n15813,TERRY SCHIAVO,Terry Schiavo was a woman involved in a highly publicized legal case regarding the withdrawal of life support and enteral nutrition due to her persistent vegetative state.,3\r\n15423,HOSPITAL INFANTIL UNIVERSITARIO NIÑO JESÚS,Hospital Infantil Universitario Niño Jesús is a children's hospital in Madrid that provides specialized pediatric care and research.,3\r\n15812,CUIDADO,\"CUIDADO refers to the concept of care, which encompasses the actions taken to support and maintain the health and well-being of individuals, particularly in medical contexts. This notion of care extends to providing support for individuals, especially at the end of life, and is viewed variably across different cultures.\",3\r\n14558,ALIMENTACIÓN POR VÍA ENTERAL,\"The method of providing nutrition directly into the gastrointestinal tract through a tube, which has been referenced since 1589.\",2\r\n15421,CONSUELO PEDRÓN GINER,\"Consuelo Pedrón Giner is a pediatric specialist and doctor at Hospital Infantil Universitario Niño Jesús in Madrid, specializing in nutrition and gastroenterology.\",2\r\n15420,ÓSCAR RUBIO CABEZAS,\"Óscar Rubio Cabezas is a pediatric specialist and researcher at Hospital Infantil Universitario Niño Jesús in Madrid, with a focus on pediatric endocrinology.\",2\r\n14301,TEOFILINA,\"Teofilina is a medication primarily used to treat respiratory diseases, including asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). Its therapeutic action can be influenced by dietary factors, as it is metabolized more quickly when a diet rich in proteins is consumed. This interaction may affect the effectiveness of the medication in managing respiratory conditions.\",2\r\n15419,ANA BELÉN MARTÍNEZ ZAZO,\"Ana Belén Martínez Zazo is a pediatric specialist and attending physician at Hospital La Moraleja in Madrid, focusing on pediatric nutrition.\",2\r\n15422,HOSPITAL LA MORALEJA,Hospital La Moraleja is a medical facility in Madrid specializing in pediatric care.,2\r\n706,ALIMENTACIÓN BÁSICA ADAPTADA,\"\"\"ALIMENTACIÓN BÁSICA ADAPTADA\"\" refers to the practice of modifying food textures and consistencies to accommodate patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. This concept includes the use of modified texture foods that are designed to be high in caloric density and rich in protein, ensuring that patients receive adequate nutrition while managing their swallowing difficulties.\",2\r\n575,AUTONOMÍA,\"Autonomía encompasses the concept of a patient's ability to perform daily activities independently, which is influenced by their nutritional status. It also signifies the right of patients to make informed decisions regarding their health care, a principle that holds particular importance in Anglo-Saxon culture. Furthermore, Autonomía is evaluated through tools such as the Mini Nutritional Assessment, which assesses a patient's capacity to live independently. Overall, Autonomía integrates both the practical aspects of daily living and the ethical dimensions of patient rights in health care decision-making.\",2\r\n15815,AUTONOMÍA DEL PACIENTE,\"AUTONOMÍA DEL PACIENTE refers to the right of patients to make informed decisions regarding their medical care and treatment. This concept emphasizes that patients have the authority to choose their course of action in healthcare matters, including critical aspects such as nutrition and hydration. The principle of patient autonomy underscores the importance of informed consent and the respect for individual preferences in the context of medical decision-making.\",8\r\n9473,MAICENA,\"Maicena is a brand of cornstarch that serves as a dietary treatment for metabolic disorders, particularly in the management of blood glucose levels. It is recognized for its properties as a polysaccharide, which makes it suitable for patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type I (GSDI). Maicena is recommended for these patients due to its slow absorption rate, which helps in maintaining stable blood glucose levels.\",2\r\n9479,DIAREAS TRANSITORIAS,\"Las diarreas transitorias son efectos secundarios leves que pueden ocurrir al introducir almidón de maíz en la dieta, pero que generalmente se resuelven espontáneamente.\",1\r\n9480,NIÑOS MAYORES,Los niños mayores de un año deben consumir al menos tres comidas al día con almidón de maíz y snacks frecuentes para mantener niveles de glucosa adecuados.,1\r\n15817,DIRECTIVAS ANTICIPADAS,\"DIRECTIVAS ANTICIPADAS are legal documents that enable individuals to outline their preferences for medical treatment in situations where they may become unable to communicate their wishes. These documents serve as a means for individuals to express their desires regarding medical care, ensuring that their treatment aligns with their values and choices, even when they cannot voice them.\",1\r\n15818,TESTAMENTO VITAL,\"The \"\"TESTAMENTO VITAL,\"\" also known as a living will, is a legal document that serves as an advance directive. It specifies an individual's preferences regarding medical treatment and life-sustaining measures in situations where they are unable to make decisions for themselves. This document outlines the person's wishes concerning their medical care, ensuring that their preferences are respected even when they cannot communicate them directly.\",1\r\n15840,PRINCIPIO DE AUTONOMÍA,El principio de autonomía es un concepto ético que sostiene que los individuos tienen el derecho a tomar decisiones sobre su propia vida y cuerpo.,1\r\n15841,PRINCIPIO DE BENEFICENCIA,El principio de beneficencia es un principio ético que implica actuar en el mejor interés del paciente y promover su bienestar.,1\r\n10732,GLYCOSADE,\"Glycosade is a modified starch that helps maintain blood glucose levels during fasting periods, particularly useful for patients with metabolic disorders.\",1\r\n14169,ALIMENTOS CON MÍNIMO RESIDUO,Los alimentos con mínimo residuo son aquellos que se deben consumir para facilitar estudios diagnósticos del tubo digestivo.,1\r\n6658,SOCIEDAD AMERICANA DE NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL,\"The \"\"SOCIEDAD AMERICANA DE NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL\"\" (ASPEN) is an organization dedicated to advancing the field of nutritional support. It provides clinical guidelines for artificial nutritional support specifically for patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation. Additionally, ASPEN offers guidelines for nutritional support tailored to hospitalized adult obese patients, with a particular focus on those undergoing bariatric surgery. Through these initiatives, ASPEN aims to enhance the quality of care and outcomes for patients requiring specialized nutritional interventions.\",1\r\n13801,SOCIEDAD EUROPEA DE NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL,ESPEN is an organization that offers clinical guidelines for artificial nutritional support in patients undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation.,1\r\n1892,BOLSA DE DRENAJE,The drainage bag connected to the feeding tube to collect gastric residuals duri